# Remedy Sans: the RemedyOS typeface, drawn as strokes on a 24-unit grid (baseline 0, x-height 14, cap height 20, ascender 21, descender -6).
# Character codes are decimal (65) or U+0041.
#
# glyph <code> adv=<units>     a character drawn here; the drawing commands follow
#   L x0,y0 x1,y1              line
#   A cx,cy rx,ry a0 a1        elliptical arc, degrees counter-clockwise from +x
#   Q x0,y0 cx,cy x1,y1        quadratic curve
#   D x,y                      dot (a round terminal)
#   F x,y x,y x,y ...          filled polygon; its edges are stroked too, so corners stay round
#   use <code> [dx,dy]         draw another character's strokes here, moved by dx,dy
#   put <mark> x,y [touch]     draw a mark at x,y, lifted clear of the stroke (touch: no gap)
#   anchor <name> x,y          where marks sit on this letter: top, bottom, ogonek, caron
# glyph <code> = <base> + <mark> [+ <mark>]
#                              the base character with each mark on the base's anchor;
#                              the advance is the base's unless adv= is given before '='
# glyph <code> = <base>        the same drawing as another character
#
# mark <name> <anchor> above|below|attach
#   An accent, drawn once with (0,0) at the anchor point. 'above' marks are drawn upward
#   from y=0 and 'below' marks downward from y=0; the build moves them away from the
#   anchor by one stroke weight plus a fixed gap, so the white space between mark and
#   letter is the same in Regular and Bold. 'attach' marks are drawn touching the anchor.
#
# Anchors and marks sit on stroke centrelines, like every other coordinate here.
# Stroke weight comes from the renderer (light 2.1, semilight 2.55, regular 3.0, semibold 3.6, bold 4.3); every terminal is round.

